Tokenome terms of use

This is the copy of https://tokenome.ai/terms that shipped with this
version of the Tokenome releases. Section 9 of the terms says the copy you
installed under governs it.

Version 1.0, effective 5 October 2026. Tokenome ("we") publishes several
things under different terms. The section that covers what you are using is
the one that applies. Plain words first, then the detail.

The short version

- The app is free to use, for work or for yourself, on as many of your own machines as you like.

- You may not resell it, host it for other people, or use it to build a competing product.

- Team is free while it is in beta. We will give at least 30 days notice before any team is charged.

- Nothing you have indexed is ever deleted or locked because of a licence.

1. The Tokenome application

The macOS app, the Linux AppImage and deb packages are licensed, not sold. We
grant you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence
to install and use the application, for personal or commercial purposes, on
any number of machines you control, at no charge.

You may not redistribute or resell the application or any part of it; rent,
lease or host it as a service for other people; remove or alter any notice in
it; or use it to build a product whose substantial purpose is capturing,
indexing or searching conversations with AI systems, or linking those
conversations to code. You may decompile or reverse engineer the application
only so far as that restriction is unenforceable under the law that applies to
you.

This covers the application as distributed. It grants no rights in the
application's own source beyond what the Business Source License grants in the
Python packages it bundles.

2. The Python packages and the Claude Code plugin

The tokenome-ai package and the tokenome-core library it depends on, and the
Claude Code plugin, whether installed from the marketplace or bundled in the
application, are licensed under the Business Source License 1.1, with an
Additional Use Grant permitting any production use other than a competing
product, and the Apache License 2.0 as the Change License four years after
each version is first published. The full text ships with those packages and
governs them; nothing here narrows it.

3. The Team server

The Tokenome team server, including the container image published as
ghcr.io/tokenome/tokenome-server, and the billing systems behind it, are
proprietary. Running the team server for your own organisation is permitted
while it is in free beta. Any other use, including offering it to other
people, needs a separate written agreement.

Beta and billing. Team is free while it is in beta, with no key to install and
no seat limit. We will tell every team on the beta at least 30 days before we
start charging, and the prices are published on the pricing page so you can
see today what it would cost later. Billing, when it starts, is annual and
invoiced; you will not be charged automatically, and there is no card on file.

If a subscription lapses. Tokenome degrades; it does not break. Search keeps
working, everything already shared keeps working, updates to projects you have
already shared keep working, and deletes keep working. What pauses is growth:
enrolling a new person, and sharing a project for the first time. Both resume
the moment a current licence is in place. We never delete your data for a
licensing reason, and there is no path in the software that does it. Whatever
is paused, the console and the command line say so plainly.

4. Your data

On a single machine, your conversations and the index built from them stay on
that machine. We have no account system and receive nothing. On Team, what
leaves a laptop is what that person opts in to share, with secrets redacted
before it goes, and it goes to a server your organisation runs. We never train
on your data. What each part of the product holds is described in the privacy
documentation.

